B.bcn=new A.b("3\u20135 mg/kg/24 hr PO \xf7 once daily\u2013BID; dosages as high as 5\u201310 mg/kg/24 hr have been used for Aspergillus prophylaxis in chronic granulomatous disease. Population pharmacokinetic data in pediatric cystic fibrosis and bone marrow transplant patients suggest an oral liquid dosage of 10 mg/kg/24 hr PO \xf7 BID or oral capsule dosage of 20 mg/kg/24 hr PO \xf7 BID to be more reliable for achieving trough plasma levels between 500 and 2000 ng/mL.",!1)
