B.cXZ=s(["IV or IM doses may cause flushing, dizziness, cardiac/respiratory arrest, hypotension, and anaphylaxis. IV or IM administration is indicated only when other routes of administration are not feasible (or in emergency situations).","Monitor prothrombin time/partial thromboplastin time. Large doses (10\u201320 mg) in newborns may cause hyperbilirubinemia and severe hemolytic anemia. Blood coagulation factors increase within 6\u201312 hr after oral doses and within 1\u20132 hr following parenteral administration. Use of higher doses for warfarin overdose may cause warfarin resistance for \u22651 wk. Concurrent administration of oral mineral oil may decrease gastrointestinal absorption of oral vitamin K.","IV injection rate not to exceed 3 mg/m\xb2/min or 1 mg/min. Protect product from light. See Chapter 21 for multivitamin preparations."],t.s)
