B.dez=s(["Use with caution in penicillin-allergic patients or in presence of renal impairment. Good Pseudomonas coverage and CSF penetration. May cause rash, liver enzyme elevations, and false-positive urine-reducing substance (e.g., Clinitest, Benedict\u2019s solution, or Fehling\u2019s solution) and Coombs test. Enzymatic glucose oxidase urinary glucose tests (e.g., Clinistix or Tes-Tape) are recommended. Probenecid increases serum ceftazidime levels. Adjust dose in renal failure (see Chapter 32). Nonconvulsive status epilepticus, neuromuscular excitability, and myoclonia may occur with elevated levels of ceftazidime."],t.s)
