B.d5H=s(["Do not use in narrow-angle glaucoma. May cause a burning sensation, behavioral disturbance, tachycardia, and loss of visual accommodation. Psychotic reactions and behavioral disturbances have been reported in children. To minimize absorption, apply pressure over nasolacrimal sac for at least 2 min. CNS and cardiovascular side effects are common with the 2% solution in children. Avoid feeding infants within 4 hr of dosing to prevent potential feeding intolerance.","Onset of action: 15\u201360 min; duration of action: 6\u201324 hr; complete recovery of accommodation may take several days for some patients. Observe patient closely for at least 30 min after dose."],t.s)
