B.dLG=s(["AVOID long-term use. Chronic antacid use is not recommended for children with GERD. Use with caution in patients with renal failure and upper GI hemorrhage.","Interferes with the absorption of several orally administered medications, including digoxin, ethambutol, indomethacin, isoniazid, naproxen, mycophenolate, tetracyclines, fluoroquinolones (e.g., ciprofloxacin), and iron. In general, do not take oral medications within 1\u20132 hr of taking aluminum dose unless specified.","May cause constipation, decreased bowel motility, encephalopathy, and phosphorus depletion."],t.s)
