B.dSj=s(["Use with caution in preexisting renal, vestibular, or auditory impairment; concomitant anesthesia or neuromuscular blockers; concomitant neurotoxic, ototoxic, or nephrotoxic drugs; sulfite sensitivity; and dehydration. Adjust dose in renal failure (see Chapter 32).","Longer dosing intervals may be necessary for neonates receiving indomethacin for PDAs and for all patients with poor cardiac output. Rapidly eliminated in patients with cystic fibrosis or burns, and in febrile neutropenic patients. CNS penetration is poor beyond early infancy.","For initial dosing in obese patients, use an adjusted body weight (ABW). ABW = ideal body weight + 0.4 (total body weight \u223c ideal body weight).","May cause ototoxicity, nephrotoxicity, neuromuscular blockade, and rash. Loop diuretics may potentiate the ototoxicity of all aminoglycoside antibiotics.","A liposomal inhalation product, Arikayce, is currently approved in adults as part of a multidrug treatment regimen for Mycobacterium avium complex (MAC) lung disease."],t.s)
