B.daK=s(["Renal elimination. Adjust dose in renal failure (see Chapter 32). Serum levels about twice those achieved with equal dose of ampicillin. Fewer GI effects, but otherwise similar to ampicillin. Side effects: rash and diarrhea. Rash may develop with concurrent EBV infection. Drug-induced enterocolitis syndrome and severe cutaneous reactions have been reported. May increase warfarin\u2019s effect by increasing INR.","High-dose regimen is recommended in respiratory infections (e.g., CAP), acute otitis media, and sinusitis, owing to increasing incidence of penicillin-resistant pneumococci. Chewable tablets may contain phenylalanine and should not be used by patients with phenylketonuria."],t.s)
