B.dbl=s(["Rash and GI disturbances are common. Leukopenia, reversible hepatotoxicity, and acute interstitial nephritis have been reported. Hematuria and azotemia have occurred in neonates and infants with high doses. May cause false-positive urinary and serum proteins.","Probenecid increases serum oxacillin levels. Tetracyclines may antagonize the bactericidal effects of oxacillin.","CSF penetration is poor unless meninges are inflamed. Use the lower end of the usual dosage range for patients with creatinine clearances <10 mL/min. Adjust dose in renal failure (see Chapter 32)."],t.s)
