B.bYb=new A.l9("\u03b21 agonist at moderate dose, \u03b11 at high dose, dopaminergic at low dose.","First-line inotrope for neonatal shock/hypotension; renal-dose effect at \u22645 mcg/kg/min is controversial in neonates.","Extravasation causes tissue necrosis \u2014 use a confirmed central or deep peripheral line. Start at 5 mcg/kg/min and titrate.","NICE / ANZNN Neonatal Handbook")
B.bY4=new A.l9("Predominantly \u03b21 agonist \u2192 improves contractility and cardiac output.","Useful in myocardial dysfunction, cardiogenic shock, post-asphyxia.","Less vasoconstrictive than dopamine. Can cause tachycardia and hypotension at high doses.","Neofax \xb7 ANZNN")
B.bY6=new A.l9("Non-selective \u03b1 and \u03b2 agonist.","Refractory shock, low cardiac output despite dopamine/dobutamine, cardiac arrest bolus.","Must be given via secure IV access. Can cause severe tissue injury if extravasated.","NRP \xb7 Neofax")
B.bY7=new A.l9("Potent \u03b11 agonist with some \u03b21 activity.","Vasoplegic (warm) septic shock \u2014 raises SVR without excessive tachycardia.","Limited but growing neonatal evidence. Requires central line ideally.","ANZNN \xb7 ESPNIC consensus")
B.bYd=new A.l9("PDE3 inhibitor \u2014 inodilator. Increases contractility and reduces SVR/PVR.","Low cardiac output syndrome, PPHN with RV dysfunction, post-cardiac surgery.","No loading dose in neonates due to hypotension risk. Infuse only. Monitor BP closely.","ESPNIC \xb7 ASE TNE 2024")
B.bYf=new A.l9("Synthetic opioid \u2014 \u03bc-receptor agonist. Analgesia + sedation.","Analgesia during mechanical ventilation, pre-procedural sedation.","Rapid onset. Chest wall rigidity with fast bolus \u2014 give slow push. Tolerance develops.","Neofax")
B.bYe=new A.l9("V1 receptor agonist \u2192 vasoconstriction via non-adrenergic pathway.","Catecholamine-refractory shock, PPHN with systemic hypotension.","Second-line agent. Monitor for hyponatraemia, ischaemic complications.","ESPNIC consensus")
B.bYg=new A.l9("\u03bc-opioid agonist.","Analgesia and sedation during ventilation; neonatal abstinence treatment.","Slower onset than fentanyl. Histamine release may drop BP. Dose per unit protocol.","Neofax \xb7 AAP")
B.bY5=new A.l9("Prostaglandin E1 (alprostadil) \u2014 keeps ductus arteriosus patent.","Duct-dependent congenital heart disease (cyanotic lesions, coarctation, HLHS).","Apnoea in 10\u201320% \u2014 be prepared to intubate. Hypotension, fever, jitteriness common.","NRP \xb7 ESC Cardiology")
B.bYa=new A.l9("Benzodiazepine \u2014 GABA-A receptor potentiation.","Seizure control (2nd/3rd line), procedural sedation, sedation on ventilator.","Avoid as routine sedation in preterm (myoclonus, poor neurodevelopmental outcomes).","Neofax \xb7 AAP")
B.bYc=new A.l9("Loop diuretic \u2014 inhibits Na-K-2Cl cotransporter in loop of Henle.","Fluid overload, heart failure, BPD chronic lung disease.","Ototoxicity with rapid infusion or concurrent aminoglycosides. Monitor K, Na, Ca.","Neofax")
B.bY9=new A.l9("NMDA receptor antagonist \u2014 dissociative anaesthesia.","Procedural analgesia/sedation, intubation premedication, refractory sedation.","Preserves respiratory drive and BP. Bronchodilator. Increases secretions.","ANZNN \xb7 Neofax")
B.bY3=new A.l9("Highly selective \u03b12 agonist \u2014 sedation without respiratory depression.","Off-label sedation on ventilator; extubation / procedural sedation.","Bradycardia and hypotension. Limited safety data in extreme preterm.","ESPNIC off-label review")
B.bY8=new A.l9("PDE5 inhibitor \u2014 pulmonary vasodilator.","PPHN unresponsive to iNO; chronic pulmonary hypertension in BPD.","Monitor systemic BP (can drop). Loading followed by maintenance infusion or enteral dose.","ESPNIC \xb7 ASE TNE 2024")
B.a4D=new A.bp(B.a59,[B.bYb,B.bY4,B.bY6,B.bY7,B.bYd,B.bYf,B.bYe,B.bYg,B.bY5,B.bYa,B.bYc,B.bY9,B.bY3,B.bY8],A.ah("bp<m,l9>"))
